      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0035" n="art0035">
        <p>I'HE EXAMINER, FRID &amp;lie, JANUARY 24 1902.</p>
        <p>[ALL RIGHTS RESERVED.)</p>
        <p>- $,</p>
        <p>'7.4Thell; Is it _Dangerous ? . CV• L - Does it mean Consumption?</p>
        <p>If the Blood is in a thin, poor state, and deficient in quantity, a cough may easily damage your lungs; you will spit blood; the wound in the lung will grow worse; presently you will be a little feverish and have night sweats; eventually burst a blood vessel, and DIE. That is how Anmmia leads to Consumption. Be careful: if a medicine purges the bowels don't on any account continue taking it if you are Anxtnic.</p>
        <p>This is how to tell if your</p>
        <p>Cough</p>
        <p>is Dangerous:</p>
        <p>Hold up a looking-glass and look at your low lip. Is it pale and bloodless? Hold down your eyelid—is the lining of it pale and blood shot? Are your hands and feet cold? These things mean Anemia. Be warned. Your Cough is dangerous. You are already weaker than you should be, and are threatened by Consumption. Do not delay; above all d not take "something cheaper " ; take</p>
