      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0090" n="art0090">
        <head>Harrier.</head>
        <p>Harrier.</p>
        <p>Eighteen members of rlie-S-a.ukey club turned out on Saturday for an ordinary run. A distance of about nine miles, over good country, was traversed, and after an interesting race T Devlin succeeded in getting home by about 300 yards in front of L Green. The same distance separated second and third (S Parsonage), the re- mainder of the pack being close up. The fixture for to-day is an inter-club race with the Broughton Harriers and a big muster is expected.</p>
        <p>Angling. At a meeting held in the Ring o' Bells, Wilderspool- road, on Monday evening, Mr William Mather in the chair,it was decided to:form a club under the title of the King Edward VII Coronation Club of Jolly Anglers to affiliate with the Warrington Angling Association, Mr Waldron was unanimously elected its first president, and Mr John Massey vice-president ; 26 members were enrolled, and a committee appointed with Mr S Foulkes as secretary, and Mr Thomas Boscow as treasurer. The committee consists of Messrs Charles Mather,Lawrence Spencer, Arthur Boscow, Joseph Shepherd and Joseph Robinson.</p>
      </div>
