      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0105" n="art0105">
        <head>LANCASHIRE RUGBY COM-</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE RUGBY COM-</p>
        <p>B!NATION.</p>
        <p>SwINToN " A" VlCTolliouS AT WILDERsPeoL. More than usual interest centred in the match between Warrington and Swinton "A" teams at Wilderspool on Saturday owing to the fact that Swinton are going strongly for the Championship of the Combination not having sus- tained a single defeat this season. The Warrington men were on their mettle on Saturday and tried hard to break the fine record of the visitors, but failed , to do so. Swintoa were very strongly represented, Jim Valentine figuring in the forwards and his brother C Valentine in the three quarter line. Another well known I player in the person of Messer appeared at half back. In the I Warrington forward ranks, Eden, Dakin and Cunningham found places. There would be three thousand spectators I round the enclosure at the kick off. The first scrimmage ended in Warrington's favour. The visitors got away, but Drown returned. Warrington worked their way into the visitors' quarter, and from a free kick Lawless failed at goal. Swinton then pressed, and from a pass 0 Valentine soored at the corner, Jim Valentine plaeing a goal, On restarting, Warrington pressed, but lengthy kicking by the Swinton Peeks toot play to half-way. Duckworth raced away, and fussed to Clare, who slipped when he had a clear field. Swin- tm then attacked again, and from a free kick Jim Valentine landed a second goal. Warrington again pressed, but failed to break through the Swinton defence. Half-tinte—Swinton 2 goals, 1 try. Warrington nil. In the second half Warrington played up vigorously but several openicgs welch presented themselves were not taken full advantage of. Clare lost a good opportunity by failing to take a pass soon after the restart and Lawless held the bail when a pass to the wing man T Knight would very pro- bably have resulted in something tangib e. The home team were penalised and Jim Valentine aeain displayed his goal- kicking abilities by landing the ball over the cross-bar. The was all the so ving in the second half and Warrington retired beaten by three goals. Oue try (nine points) to nil.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0106" n="art0106">
        <head>LANCASHIdE JUNIOR LEAGUE.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIdE JUNIOR LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>LArCHFORD RINGERS V. ST. HELENS SHAMROCKS. This match was pisyei at St. Helens on Saturday. Shamrock' won the toss and played down hill. The Rangers were soon defending their line and from a good passing movement t•-.,e ball went to Crevor wno rounded all opposi- tion and scored a splendid try for the Shamrocks, Hall con- verting. On the kick-off the Rangers got going and some good passing ended in Burton scoring, Hewitt kicking the goal. The second half was evenly contested, Hewitt kicked a splendid goal which placed the Rangers ahead, and they won a good game by 7 points to 5 points. Fillingham at full back played a splendid game for the Rangers. Spencer at three-quarters and Bramhall at half back are also worthy of special mention. All the forwards played a good game.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0107" n="art0107">
        <head>ASSOC! ATION FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>ASSOC! ATION FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON ST. PETERS v. WIDNES ALBERTS. Played on the ground of the former before a moderate at- tendance. The weather was favourable and the ground in good condition. St Peter's played a forcing') game through- out the fi rat half, and the Widnes defenders had a lively time of it. In the last half a fine run down by Phenix on the right wing put Craddock on the alert, who. after a bit of good play scored a fine god!, the game ending in a victory for St by goal ;</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
        <head>Lancashire League.</head>
        <p>Lancashire League.</p>
        <p>EARLEST3WN V. WIGAN UNITED,</p>
        <p>Considerable Interest was centred in this return League match. which took place on Mesne's Ground, harlestown, on Saturday, There were about 2,000 spectators present and the final score after a splendid game was :—Eariestown 1 ; Wigan 1.</p>
