        <p>°Two plints deduoted for breach of rulee. " WARRINGTON GUARDIAN" V. FRODSHAM PARISI/ OFIVRCII At Warrington,on Saturday. After a well contested game Prodsharn retired victors by ole goal to nil. ituNcons PAEISB Cuteon v BEWdET ALL SAINT3'. Played. at Warrington on Saturday The visitors won the toss, and elected to play down the field. Wiliamion made a good dribble, passing to (.1 Borrows who nicely landed the ball between the poets. Shortly site.wsrds one of the Bewsey forwards got possession. taking the ball from one end of the field to the other, and only just missing his shot by a few inches. The homesters obtained a corner kick by which they experienced very hard lines. the ball falling on the crossbar. Bewsey scored their first goal from a com- bined rush just before half-time. Wright had no possible chance against them. Score at half time—Runcorn Parish Church, one goal Bewsey All Saints, one goal. The game was recommenced omit Bewsey immediately began pressing taking the ball within a yard of the goal, when, unfortun- ately, one 01 the visitors "hooded it. A penalty resulted from whims th, homestors were unable to score, Wright ' meeting the shot and saving in splendid style. Bewsey scored their second and third goals in quick sumession. the final score teing a w.n for the hOma team by threa goals to one.</p>
