      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-01-24_WidnesExaminer_art0109" n="art0109">
        <head>LANCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE JUNIOR COMBINATION.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE JUNIOR COMBINATION.</p>
        <p>No. of Matches Goals Goals Played. Won. an. Lost. for ag't Pts. Wilderspool Central 18 12 2 ... 4 ... 60... 23.„ 26 Weston Church Re've 17 ... 11 ... 1 ... 5 ... 45... 31... 23 Widnes St. Mary's l4 ... 9 ... 4 ... 1 ... 26... 11... 22 Weston Church l7 ... 11 ... 0 ... 6 ... 32,.. 18... 22 Howley l4 ... 9 ... 1 4 ... 24,.. 20... 19 Appleton White Star 16 ... 8 3 ... 5 ... 33... 22... 1 9 Halton View Juniors 14 ... 9 ... 5 ... 30... 17... 18 Mariners' Church Widnes Albert.. 37 ... 4 ... 5 ... 8 ... 1.6... 31... 13 West Bank Juniors ... 16 ... 5 ... 2 g ... 18... 34... 12 Frod,ham Parish 04 10 ... 5... 1... 4 ... 23... 13... 11 Penketh !WARM:PearI Ji.ltilohs V. WILIDER9POoL CENTRAL. Played on the ground of the first named. he visitors started, and after a series or attacks Grour•ds beat lilley with an easy shot. The juniors broke away, but Dawson cleared out of danger. Knight dashed along tip field and passed to Donald, but this player missed a grand chance to score. From a corner the Juniors equalized. Half-time. Wilderspool, one ; Juniors, one. On restarting the visitors pressed, the locals defending In fine style for some time. Wilderspool broke away at times, but their shooting was erratic. Cowell ran along the wing and passed to Knight, but this player missing the ball, Inglis put the leather through. Evans dribbled past several opponents and his. final shot beat the home custodian. The Juniors were now on the defensive, and but for Fleming the score would have been considerably greater. Final • Wilderspool Central, three goals; Warrington Juniors, one pal •</p>
