        <p>CtOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON TO N.} CONTRACTORS. The PAVING and SEWERAGE COMMITTEE of the Council of the Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive TENDERS for the construction ot about 338 Lineal yards of Sin. Stoneware Pipe Sewer, and 37 Lineal yards of 91n, Cast Iron Pipe Sewer, and other works in connection therewith. Drawings, specifications, etc.. may be seen, and forms of tender, bills of quantities, and all further information obtained at the office of the Borough surveyor, Town Hall, , on and after THURSDAY NEXT, the 16th instant, at which ' place tenders must be delivered on or before 12 o'clock on MONDAY, the 27th day of JANUARY, 1932. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. THOMAS LONGDIN, Borough Engineer and Surveyor. Borough Engineer and Surveyor's office, January 10th. 1902.</p>
        <p>COIINTY BOROUGEI OF WARRINGTON.— THE HEALTH COMMITTEE of the COUNTY BOROUGH of Warrington REQUIRE THE SERVICES of a MATRON for their Hospital for Infectious Diseases. She must not be less than 30 nor more than 40 years of age. She must be used to the routine of hospitals as well as accustomed to the control of servants and to domestic management. Salary £5O per annum with board, lodging, washing and indoor Uniform. Applications with copies of not more than three recent testimonials to be sent in on or before the Bth of February 1902 to the undersigned. J. LYON WHITTLE. Town Clerk. Town Hall, Warrington, 17th January, 1902.</p>
