        <p>Programme for 1902.' The committee ot the above Association have just recently issued their programme of events for the ensu- ing year. These fixtures and the various conditions under which they will be decided are as follows : BENEVOLENT FUND ANGLING CONTEST.—Saturday, June 21st, Worsley Canal. ASSOCIATION ANGLING CONTESTS. —lSt contest, RlM'S- day, August 111th, Shropshire Union Canal, Beesten Castle; 2nd contest. Saturday August 16:h, river Weaver, at Vale Royal. CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL CONTEST.—(OpeD to all mem- bers of the Association), Saturciay, August 23rd, river 1 Weaver at Vale Royal. - SHIELD COMPETITION.—Ist contest; Saturday, August 30th, river Weaver Barrow's Lock, near Northwich. 2nd contest, Saturday, September 13:h, river Weaver, at Vale Royal. 3rd contest and final, Siturday, September 20th, Shropshire Union Canal at Tattenhall- road. Angling Clubs affiliated with the above Associa tiers are entitled to compete, and can enter as many teams (consisting of six members each) as they choo3e. THE JUVENILE CONTEST.—Saturday, September 6th, at Beatles, will be a roving match. THE COMMITTEE Maxcu.—Saturday, September 27th at Beatley will be a roving match. The prize distribu- tion will be undertaken on Monday, October 27th.</p>
